{
  "name": "Matrioshka Brain",
  "icon": "theoreticalsciences:matrioshka_brain",
  "category": "theoreticalsciences:minds",
  "sortnum": 43,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:matrioshka_brain",
      "title": "Matrioshka Brain",
      "text": "Nested shells of computronium around a star, each living on the waste heat of the one inside. It thinks; I gain Insight.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 5$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "This controller is too complex for a crafting grid. Build it on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts.$(br2)The idea is Robert Bradbury's, from 1997: a Dyson sphere turned into a computer, the largest mind a single star could power."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Every computation the brain finishes grants its owner $(thing)5 Insight$() - the brain does my science for me. I have started leaving it questions overnight."
    },
